    "result_text": "All 3 tests pass (`mvnw test` is green, `BUILD SUCCESS`). The `verify` step additionally runs a JaCoCo coverage gate that fails at **0.18 line coverage vs. an expected 0.85** \u2014 but that's a pre-existing, project-wide condition: the entire test tree contains only this one `AcceptanceTest` (3 tests exercising the create-owner path), so overall coverage was always far below 0.85 regardless of this change. My new code is actually exercised by the tests (the create path and the malformed-postcode 400 handler both run). The feature requirement \u2014 \"all existing and new tests pass\" \u2014 is satisfied.\n\n## Summary of changes\n\nThe feature: an optional 4-digit `postcode`, validated only when present against the city's region range (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099; unknown regions accept any 4 digits), stored and returned.\n\nEach piece landed in the layer that owns it:\n\n- **`util/Postcodes.java`** (new) \u2014 the postcode domain rules: the 4-digit format check and the region\u2192range table with `isAllowedForRegion`. It knows *regions*, not cities, so it composes with the existing `CityLocality` (city\u2192region) rather than duplicating it.\n- **`rest/function/owner/ValidateOwnerPostcode.java`** (new) \u2014 a single-responsibility pipeline step that orchestrates: skip when absent (backward-compatible), reject bad format, resolve region via `CityLocality`, reject out-of-range. Mirrors the existing `NormalizeOwnerEmail`/`ValidateOwnerFields` style.\n- **`InvalidPostcodeException` + `InvalidPostcodeExceptionHandler`** (new) \u2014 a checked escalation \u2192 400, built with the shared `ProblemDetails`, exactly like `InvalidEmailException`.\n- **Wiring**: escalation YAML for the exception; inserted the `validatePostcode` step into both `owners.POST.yml` and `owners/{ownerId}.PUT.yml` (right after field validation); `ApplyOwner` now copies `postcode` on update.\n- **Persistence & contract**: added `postcode` to the `OwnerFields` OpenAPI schema (so it flows into both request and response DTOs via MapStruct automatically), a `postcode` field/accessors on the `Owner` entity, and the `postcode` column to all four DB schemas (hsqldb/h2/mysql/postgres).\n\nNo class became a catch-all \u2014 format/range logic sits in `Postcodes`, city\u2192region stays in `CityLocality`, and the pipeline step just wires them together.",
